The [original #4471 page](/kb/incidents/4471) says that all reports are one known parser
bug with one fix queued. Its rendered cause table contradicts that claim. The export
establishes two independent failure paths. This review uses the export dated 2026-10-04,
plus the later engineering update on the course page; the export itself is not a live feed.

## Engineering update: different closure outcomes

The [course desk update](https://hq.mega.dev/challenges/what-it-shows) reports that
**#4471 closed on 2026-10-05**:

- **Parser: fixed.** Engineering reports `fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales`.
  The [parser issue](https://github.com/michalkoscallegro/mega_dev_s01e03/issues/1) is closed
  as **completed**.
- **Hint: won't fix.** The **booking-v3 form was retired**, so the
  [hint issue](https://github.com/michalkoscallegro/mega_dev_s01e03/issues/2) is closed as
  **not planned**, not as a shipped hint fix.

Both issues are closed, but only one defect was fixed. These outcomes come from the course's
engineering update, not a product patch implemented in this KB repository. The historical
report counts below remain unchanged.

## What the desk should track

<CauseTable ticket={4471} {issueLinks} />

### Shared parser: month first instead of the tenant's date convention

The [parser issue](https://github.com/michalkoscallegro/mega_dev_s01e03/issues/1) covers day-first
tenants using app or email, and booking-v2 forms. For example, R-41200 from harbour.dental
describes 7 April becoming 4 July. The tenant is en-GB even if a reporter's browser is set
otherwise. R-41205 from morrow.tax is an app report with tenant fr-FR, despite browser en-US
and intake tag hint. It belongs to parser.

Interpret the original input using the tenant convention, and verify the resulting date.
Preserve month-first behavior. Do not mark the independent form-hint issue fixed when this
parser is corrected.

### booking-v3: the displayed hint disagrees with form parsing

The [hint issue](https://github.com/michalkoscallegro/mega_dev_s01e03/issues/2) covers form reports
from alder.physio (de-DE), copper.studio (es-ES), and pale.harbour (pt-PT). They run booking-v3,
which displays MM/DD/YYYY while reading input day first. R-41230 describes 6 January becoming
1 June; intake incorrectly tagged it parser. Following that hint with 01/06/2026 reproduces
the mismatch.

The original corrective option was to generate the hint from the same tenant convention
used to read the input. Engineering instead retired booking-v3 and chose won't fix.
App and email reports from these tenants are not automatically hint reports: channel matters.

## Counting and evidence

<IncidentSummary />

Counts are computed from the export by the supplied code, not copied from intake labels.
`uniqueById` removes overlapping export rows; `causeOf` uses channel plus the authoritative
tenant locale and installed form. `dayFirst` asks Intl.DateTimeFormat for that locale's
date-part order. `locales.ts` resolves the tenant directory, not `meta.browserLocale`.
Missing tenant configuration is unplaced, never a reason to guess or merge by subject.

## When it happened

<QueueTimeline ticket={4471} />

Reports arrived before the desk merged them, and continued after it did. A large known
ticket and a queued fix are not evidence of resolution. Compare receivedAt with mergedAt
before interpreting a spike.

## Change the running desk rule, not just this incident

[Decision 0002](/kb/decisions/0002-dedupe-by-cause) replaces subject-only merging.
[Current triage](/kb/triage/dedupe) now asks for product, tenant configuration, entry point,
and evidence of a shared cause. Equal subjects can hide different defects; different
subjects can describe the same defect. Unknowns stay separate for investigation.

Decision 0001 remains unchanged as the historical accepted decision. This incident is an
example of why it is superseded, not permission to apply a scheduling-specific classifier
blindly to every product the support desk handles.

